      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "INQUISITOR (1) looks ready to win after consecutive BM58 fourths at Sunshine Coast, the latest when he picked up nicely from well back behind Groening. He now gets back to a BM55 and has two wins plus a placing from seven previous starts at around 1470m, which gives him the clearest overall profile despite the top weight. SOUTHOFTHEBORDER (6) is the main danger with class relief from a BM58 at Ipswich and a record that includes a placing at this distance, though his latest run was plain enough to leave a small query. NITROGEN (3) has been racing consistently, including a close Emerald third before his Taroom fourth, but he rises from a picnic BM50 into stronger BM55 company. VON BEE (4) has to rebound from a poor Kilcoy run, yet his previous second at this venue and the drop from BM60 grade keep him in the place and each-way mix.",
